    "https://jobs.hrc.pdx.edu/postings/50415": {
      "title": "AY26-27 Geology Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Portland State Careers | AY26-27 Geology Adjunct Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Sustainability Virtual Campus Tour Rankings Total Compensation Calculator AY26-27 Geology Adjunct Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Announcement Position Details Proposed Start Date 09/16/2026 Working Title AY26-27 Geology Adjunct Instructor Department 221100 - GLG Geology Position Number D97750 Representation AP - AFT, Local 3571 Position Summary Brief Description of PSU/School/Dept Portland State University, with its 49-acre downtown campus, is a comprehensive public university enrolling 20,000 students. PSU seeks to meet the needs of its increasingly diverse population through its curriculum, research, and community service activities. PSU’s mission is to provide access through the life span to a quality liberal education for undergraduates and an appropriate array of professional and graduate programs. Geology is the study of Earth and other planetary bodies; their composition, structure, and evolution. The Portland State University Geology Department excels at both teaching and research, partnering with local businesses, government, regional universities and K-12 schools. We are situated in the Pacific Northwest, a dynamic geologic environment. We capitalize on our unique location and the diversity of our faculty and student body. Position Summary Portland State University’s Geology Department invites applications for local Adjunct Instructors with expertise in core areas of Geology and teaching experience to teach undergraduate sections of courses in Geology. Minimum Qualifications M.S. or M.A. in Geology (or closely related field). Previous teaching experience. Applicant must reside in Oregon or SW Washington Preferred Qualifications M.S. or M.A. in (or closely related field). Previous teaching experience. Previous experience teaching large undergraduate classes in Geology. Key Cultural Competencies • Creates an environment that acknowledges, encourages and celebrates differences. • Functions and communicates effectively and respectfully within the context of varying beliefs, behaviors, orientations, identities and cultural backgrounds. • Seeks opportunities to gain experience working and collaborating in diverse, multicultural, and inclusive settings with a willingness to change for continual improvement • Adheres to all PSU’s policies including the policies on Prohibited Discrimination & Harassment and the Professional Standards of Conduct. Environmental Stewardship Contributes to a culture of environmental stewardship, practices resource conservation, and actively works toward achieving long-term sustainability goals. Required Professional Standards of Conduct At Portland State University, all employees are expected to conduct themselves in a professional manner which maintains a safe, respectful, and productive environment for faculty, students, administrators, and staff. It is the responsibility of every member of the Portland State University community to conduct themselves in accordance with our PSU Professional Standards of Conduct which are available at www.pdx.edu/hr/professional-standards-conduct. Compensation Adjunct faculty members are paid per credit hour per the AFT Collective Bargaining Agreement which can be found at https://www.pdx.edu/academic-affairs/academic-unions#psufa Application Instructions Additional Information Does this position require the employee to drive a motor vehicle? No Background Check Required Yes Search Details Posting Close Date Projected Close Date for Posting Open Until Filled Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Copyright © Portland State University Equal Opportunity Employer/Veterans/Disabled To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
