    "https://jobs.hrc.pdx.edu/postings/50523": {
      "title": "Position Announcement",
      "description": "Portland State Careers | Temporary Clerical Pool-Summer 2026 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Sustainability Virtual Campus Tour Rankings Total Compensation Calculator Temporary Clerical Pool-Summer 2026 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Portland State University collects applications on an ongoing basis for the Temporary Clerical pool. Postings are typically updated at the beginning of each term for periodic departmental needs. Please verify your information with each new posting if you wish to remain in the Temporary Clerical pool. If a department needs temporary assistance, you may be contacted directly. Please, no phone calls. Temporary employees are eligible for use of the PSU library and gym facilities. Temporary employees are not eligible for any vacation, health benefits, or reduced tuition. Most temporary assignments last 30 to 90 days while recruitment takes place to fill a regular position, or for a special project. Temporary employees are limited to 1,040 hours within a given twelve months. PAY PERIOD for temporary employees extends from the 16th of one month to the 15th of the following month, with payment on the last business day of the month (i.e., work from Dec 16 to Jan 15 is paid approximately Jan 31). If you are selected as a temporary employee, this in no way implies an appointment to any regular status position at PSU. In order to compete for a regular status position, you must apply for that position if/when it is open for recruitment. Portland State University is an Affirmative Action, Equal Opportunity institution and welcomes applications from diverse candidates and candidates who support diversity. Position Announcement Position Details Proposed Start Date 06/16/2026 Classification Title Office Specialist 2 Working Title Temporary Clerical Pool-Summer 2026 Department 600300 - HRC Human Resource Center Position Number TBD Representation OP - SEIU/OPEU Local 503 Position FTE Variable based on the position, up to 1.0 End date, if applicable Position Summary Brief Description of PSU/School/Dept Portland State University is Oregon’s most affordable public research university, located in the heart of one of America’s most dynamic cities. Our mission to “let knowledge serve the city” reflects our dedication to turning ideas into action — in Portland and around the world. The city is our campus, giving students unmatched access to career connections, a vibrant cultural scene and hands-on learning experiences with hundreds of community partners. More than 20,000 students from all backgrounds bring diverse perspectives to our classrooms and campus life, from the tree-lined Park Blocks to the bustling Urban Plaza and state-of-the-art science labs. We are proud of our world-class faculty, groundbreaking research and international reputation for excellence in sustainability, community engagement and innovation. Position Summary Temporary clerical employees are periodically hired for a variety of clerical and administrative needs across campus. Minimum Qualifications from Classification Two years of general clerical experience. One year of which included typing, word processing, or other experience generating documents; OR An Associate’s degree in Office Occupations or Office Technology; OR Graduation from a private school of business with a Certificate in Office Occupations or Office Technology AND one year of general clerical experience. Note: College courses in Office Occupations or Office Technology will substitute for the required experience on a year-for-year basis. Additional Minimum Qualifications for this Position Required qualifications will vary by assignment, but may include: Significant clerical skills and experience; Excellent reception and customer service skills and experience; Strong computer skills, including word processing, spreadsheets, etc.; Strong written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Will vary by assignment. May include: Bookkeeping, budget monitoring experience; 10-key by touch; Cashiering experience. Key Cultural Competencies Creates an environment that acknowledges, encourages and celebrates differences. Functions and communicates effectively and respectfully within the context of varying beliefs, behaviors, orientations, identities and cultural backgrounds. Seeks opportunities to gain experience working and collaborating in diverse, multicultural, and inclusive settings with a willingness to change for continual improvement. Adheres to all PSU policies including the policies on Prohibited Discrimination & Harassment and the Professional Standards of Conduct. Environmental Stewardship Contributes to a culture of environmental stewardship, practices resource conservation, and actively works toward achieving long-term sustainability goals. Work Days/Hours Usually Monday-Friday, hours will vary based on position Total Compensation Range & Benefits Statement The hourly rate will depend on the position to which the employee is hired. The salary rate for this position will be between $19.36 and $21.91 per hour. Temporary employees are not eligible for benefits. Application Instructions Additional Information Additional Application Instructions (deadlines, etc.) Portland State University collects applications on an ongoing basis for the Temporary Clerical pool. Postings are typically updated at the beginning of each term for periodic departmental needs. Please verify your information with each new posting if you wish to remain in the Temporary Clerical pool. If a department needs temporary assistance, you may be contacted directly. Please, no phone calls. Temporary employees are eligible for use of the PSU library and gym facilities. Temporary employees are not eligible for any vacation, health benefits, or reduced tuition. Most temporary assignments last 30 to 90 days while recruitment takes place to fill a regular position, or for a special project. Temporary employees are limited to 1,040 hours within a given twelve months. PAY PERIOD for temporary employees extends from the 16th of one month to the 15th of the following month, with payment on the last business day of the month (i.e., work from Dec 16 to Jan 15 is paid approximately Jan 31). If you are selected as a temporary employee, this in no way implies an appointment to any regular status position at PSU . In order to compete for a regular status position, you must apply for that position if/when it is open for recruitment. Portland State University is an Affirmative Action, Equal Opportunity institution and welcomes applications from diverse candidates and candidates who support diversity. Background Check Required Yes If you have questions Please email the employment team at employment@pdx.edu Search Details Posting Close Date 09/16/2026 Application screening begins Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have PSU work experience?  (if \"yes\", please show in the work history section of your application). yes no * Do you have experience working in higher education? Yes No * Do you have experience working in Banner? Yes No * Do you have reception experience including greeting guests or customers and answering multi-line phones? Yes No * Please describe any bookkeeping experience you have. Include accounting software you have used. [indicate \"n/a\" if applicable] (Open Ended Question) * How did you first find out about this position? PSU Website Indeed.com HERCJobs Urban League of Portland Hispanic Metropolitan Chamber Oregon Employment Department Social Media Person Referral Career Builder Glass Door Other - Please describe in the next Question If you selected Other, please describe. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Copyright © Portland State University Equal Opportunity Employer/Veterans/Disabled To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
