    "https://jobs.hrc.pdx.edu/postings/50584": {
      "title": "Position Announcement",
      "description": "Portland State Careers | K14 Workforce Program Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Sustainability Virtual Campus Tour Rankings Total Compensation Calculator K14 Workforce Program Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include the names, email addresses and phone numbers for 3 professional references. We encourage you to apply, even if you do not check every box on the preferred qualifications list. We value potential, diverse perspectives, and the ability to build strong partnerships. Position Announcement Position Details Proposed Start Date 10/01/2026 Classification Title Academic Services Rank Working Title K14 Workforce Program Manager Department 270101 - EAS MCECS Dean Maseeh College Position Number D91315 Representation AU - AAUP Renewable Renewable End date, if applicable 01/31/2029 Position FTE 1.0 Tenure Status N - not applicable Position Summary Brief Description of PSU/School/Dept Portland State University is Oregon’s most innovative, diverse, and affordable public research university, located in one of the nation’s most desirable places to live, and the Maseeh College of Engineering and Computer Science is your testing ground for putting new ideas into action. We believe in involving everyone—from freshmen to faculty to community—in solving the problems facing our region and our world. Maseeh College includes five departments, 132 faculty members, and more than 2,700 students. We offer academic programs that provide transformative opportunities within the classroom and beyond. Our faculty includes six National Science Foundation ( NSF ) CAREER Award winners and two members of the National Academy of Engineering. When you join our college, you’ll be at the heart of an intellectually-challenging, personally rewarding, and purposefully inclusive environment, connected to Portland’s “silicon forest,” a nexus of growing, innovative industries and agencies. Position Summary The K14 Workforce Program Manager is responsible for the coordination of pre-college preparation initiatives and the development of K-14 partnerships. These efforts are designed to align with the strategic workforce areas identified by the Maseeh College. This is a grant funded position driven by two major funding milestones, serving as Oregon’s higher education partner in the NNME -funded PINES network and a $1 million grant to expand semiconductor career pathways through the state of Oregon. We are seeking a dynamic, organized, and collaborative professional to drive these initiatives forward. Based in the Maseeh College Dean’s Office, this role will serve as the operational backbone for our semiconductor and microelectronics grant portfolios, with the opportunity to continue past this grant with new funding secured. Serving as a crucial bridge between Maseeh College, K-12, and community college partners, this role drives dual-credit curriculum alignment, manages formal articulation agreements, and acts as a primary district liaison with deep insight into CTE pathways and school operations. The position actively coordinates workforce initiatives working with regional STEM hubs and nonprofit partners to promote high-demand semiconductor and engineering careers. Operationally, the coordinator provides end-to-end grant project management, fiscal tracking, and administrative support while overseeing teacher professional development, high school summer camps, and college internships. Additionally, the role maintains transparent communication across education and community stakeholders through strategic marketing, website maintenance, and media content collection. This position is an exceptional fit for a former Career and Technical Education ( CTE ) or engineering teacher, career counselor, or educational pathway specialist . The ideal candidate deeply understands K12 district ecosystems, community colleges, and knows how to guide students toward high-wage technical careers, and possesses the pedagogical or advisory insight needed to align high school coursework with college-level credit. This is a 1.0 FTE grant funded position, reporting to the Assistant Dean for Inclusive Innovation. In accordance with the AAUP collective bargaining agreement this position is open only to current PSU AAUP academic professionals. Article 17 Section 11 refers: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1M06dEVNc5Um7oaxRBeZvfQd2dtC6L4jS/view # INTERNAL Minimum Qualifications Seasoned knowledge and expertise in principles, concepts, and practices in designated field typically obtained through a Bachelor’s degree and 4 to 6 years of professional experience or Master’s degree with 2+ years of experience within functional area. Knowledge permits the employee to plan steps for and carry out multiphase projects and to modify techniques to solve a wide range of problems. Strong commitment to equity and inclusion Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in STEM outreach and/or pedagogy Experience with project management Experience with K12 STEM ecosystem in Oregon Experience with data analysis Key Cultural Competencies Create an environment that acknowledges, encourages, and celebrates differences. Function and communicate effectively and respectfully within the context of varying beliefs, behaviors, orientations, identities, and cultural backgrounds. Seek opportunities to gain experience working and collaborating in diverse, multicultural, and inclusive settings with a willingness to change for continual improvement. Adhere to all of PSU’s policies including the policies on Prohibited Discrimination & Harassment and the Professional Standards of Conduct. Environmental Stewardship Contributes to a culture of environmental stewardship, practices resource conservation, and actively works toward achieving long-term sustainability goals. Work Days/Hours TBD Total Compensation Range & Benefits Statement Salary is dependent on several factors, and new employees will typically start around the Q1 level to allow for later growth within the salary band. PSU has a structured process for determining starting compensation, taking into account years of related experience, applicable skills, knowledge and abilities, market parity, and internal equity. The starting annual salary for this position will be between $66,696 – $77,000 but may be negotiated above this rate dependent upon the factors above, the budget of the hiring department, and approval from HR. An excellent benefits package includes 95% premium paid healthcare; a generous retirement and vacation package; and reduced tuition rates for employee, spouse or dependent at any of the Oregon University System schools : https://www.pdx.edu/human-resources/benefits-overview Please visit our total compensation calculator to see the full value of our benefits package : https://www.pdx.edu/human-resources/psu-total-compensation-calculator. Application Instructions Additional Information In accordance with the AAUP collective bargaining agreement this position is open only to current PSU AAUP academic professionals. Article 17 Section 11 refers: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1M06dEVNc5Um7oaxRBeZvfQd2dtC6L4jS/view #internal Additional Application Instructions (deadlines, etc.) Please include the names, email addresses and phone numbers for 3 professional references. We encourage you to apply, even if you do not check every box on the preferred qualifications list. We value potential, diverse perspectives, and the ability to build strong partnerships. Does this position require the employee to drive a motor vehicle? No Background Check Required Yes Position End Date (if applicable) If you have questions Search Details Posting Close Date 09/17/2026 Projected Close Date for Posting Closes Application screening begins 09/16/2026 Quick Link https://jobs.hrc.pdx.edu/postings/50573 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position is open only to current PSU AAUP academic professionals. Are you currently employed as an AAUP academic professional? Yes No * How did you first find out about this position? PSU Website Indeed.com HERCJobs Urban League of Portland Hispanic Metropolitan Chamber Oregon Employment Department Social Media Person Referral Career Builder Glass Door Other - Please describe in the next Question If you selected Other, please describe. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Professional References Optional Documents Copyright © Portland State University Equal Opportunity Employer/Veterans/Disabled To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.hrc.pdx.edu/postings/49704": {
      "title": "2026-27 Adjunct Instructor of Human Resource Management",
      "description": "Portland State Careers | 2026-27 Adjunct Instructor of Human Resource Management - The School of Business Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Sustainability Virtual Campus Tour Rankings Total Compensation Calculator 2026-27 Adjunct Instructor of Human Resource Management - The School of Business Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Announcement Position Details Proposed Start Date 09/16/2026 Working Title 2026-27 Adjunct Instructor of Human Resource Management - The School of Business Department 250001 - SBA Deans Office Position Number D97728 Representation AP - AFT, Local 3571 Position Summary Brief Description of PSU/School/Dept Position Summary The School of Business at PSU is currently collecting applications for a future opening. This position would teach courses in Human Resource Management within The School of Business undergraduate or graduate programs. Courses may be taught in person, online, and/or in a hybrid format. We will contact qualified candidates when a suitable opening becomes available. All adjunct candidates are required to be living in either Oregon or Washington for the academic year 2026-2027. Minimum Qualifications Masters Degree All adjunct candidates are required to be living in either Oregon or Washington for the academic year 2026-2027. Preferred Qualifications Key Cultural Competencies Creates an environment that acknowledges, encourages and celebrates differences. Functions and communicates effectively and respectfully within the context of varying beliefs, behaviors, orientations, identities and cultural backgrounds. Seeks opportunities to gain experience working and collaborating in diverse, multicultural, and inclusive settings with a willingness to change for continual improvement Adheres to all PSU’s policies including the policies on Prohibited Discrimination & Harassment and the Professional Standards of Conduct. Environmental Stewardship Contributes to a culture of environmental stewardship, practices resource conservation, and actively works toward achieving long-term sustainability goals. Required Professional Standards of Conduct At Portland State University, all employees are expected to conduct themselves in a professional manner which maintains a safe, respectful, and productive environment for faculty, students, administrators, and staff. It is the responsibility of every member of the Portland State University community to conduct themselves in accordance with our PSU Professional Standards of Conduct which are available at https://www.pdx.edu/human-resources/professional-standards-conduct-policy. Compensation Adjunct faculty members are paid per credit hour per the PSUFA Collective Bargaining Agreement which can be found at https://www.pdx.edu/academic-affairs/academic-unions. The current rate as of 9/16/2026 is $1,360/credit. Application Instructions Additional Information Does this position require the employee to drive a motor vehicle? No Background Check Required Yes Search Details Posting Close Date Projected Close Date for Posting Open Until Filled Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you interested in teaching online classes? Yes, and I have prior experience Yes, and I do not have prior experience No * Do you have a Master's degree? Yes No * How did you first find out about this position? PSU Website Indeed.com HERCJobs Urban League of Portland Hispanic Metropolitan Chamber Oregon Employment Department Social Media Person Referral Career Builder Glass Door Other - Please describe in the next Question If you selected Other, please describe. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Copyright © Portland State University Equal Opportunity Employer/Veterans/Disabled To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
